/// `std-console`: The standard streams.
/// Implemented: `std.console`, `library/std/src/console.gandr`, holds `print`, which writes one line to standard output through the console's root capability; `std.authority`'s `console` opens that capability from the authority `gandr run` gives `main`, and `corpus/model/effects/hello.gandr` prints through it.
/// Not implemented: standard error and standard input, which the host's `Console` interface lacks, and which #2970 owes; a capability a handler's scope introduces cannot reach `print`, which takes a capability of no region.

// `Authority`, `console`.
import "../../../library/std/src/authority.gandr";

// `print`.
import "../../../library/std/src/console.gandr";

/// A greeting through the console that `main` opens from its authority.
pub def hello(authority : Authority) -> [Console] Unit {
  print(console(authority), "hello, world!")
}
